    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0919" n="819" xml:id="pg819"/>

                <head>No. 520.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. de
                    Pestel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 2,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th ultimo informing me of the recognition of the
                    principality of Roumania by His Majesty the King of the Netherlands, and in
                    reply it is, proper to state that the President has caused such steps to be
                    taken on the part of the Government of the United States in a like direction as
                    will, it is hoped, result in the establishment of diplomatic relations with the
                    Prince of Roumania at no very distant day. To this end I have already addressed
                    the proper committees in Congress.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
